# 🎯 Important Interview Points

✅ BERT uses **Encoder-only Transformers**.

✅ Every encoder block has:

- 1 Multi-Head Self-Attention module
- 2 Layer Normalization layers
- 2 Residual Connections
- 2 Feed Forward Linear layers
- 2 Dropout layers
- 1 GELU activation

✅ Hidden size remains **768** throughout the encoder.

✅ The Feed Forward Network temporarily expands the hidden dimension from **768 → 3072 → 768**.

✅ All 12 encoder blocks have the same architecture but learn different parameters.

---

# 🎯 60-Second Interview Answer

> "A BERT-Base encoder block takes an input of shape `(sequence_length × 768)`. It first computes Query, Key, and Value using three learned linear projections, splits them into 12 attention heads of dimension 64, computes scaled dot-product self-attention, concatenates the head outputs, and applies a final output projection. This is followed by dropout, a residual connection, and Layer Normalization. The output then passes through a two-layer Feed Forward Network that expands the hidden dimension from 768 to 3072, applies a GELU activation, projects back to 768, and again applies dropout, a residual connection, and Layer Normalization. The final output has the same shape as the input and is passed to the next encoder block. This sequence is repeated across all 12 encoder blocks in BERT-Base."
